.TH BSKYTEST 1
.SH NAME
bskytest \- test the #C/curl/JSON path bsky(1) depends on
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bskytest
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Bskytest
calls
.IR bsky (1)'s
own in-process
.B pubtest()
seam \(em a test-only entry point, the same justification
.BR run() 's
own comment gives for existing at all (see
.IR eqnorbitaltest (1)
and
.IR orbitviewtest (1)
for the same pattern applied elsewhere in this tree).
.B Pubtest
fetches
.BR app.bsky.actor.getProfile ,
a real, public, unauthenticated Bluesky endpoint, through the exact
.B curl()
and JSON-decoding path
.BR bsky (1)'s
own
.B login()
and
.B timeline()
use, and checks that the decoded handle is exactly
.BR bsky.app .
Because the endpoint needs no session, this exercises the whole
transport \(em
.BR #C ,
the host's
.IR curl (1),
real TLS, and this tree's
.B json
library reading the reply back \(em without a credentials file or
any live account.
.PP
.B Postpubtest
calls
.BR login() ,
the one caller of
.BR curl() 's
request-body path and of
.BR jsonquote() ,
with a deliberately bogus handle and password. It cannot reach a real
account, but the real server can only answer with a real, well-formed
error
.RB ( AuthenticationRequired ,
or
.B RateLimitExceeded
if this exact test has already run often enough in one session to
trip the server's own rate limiter) if the JSON body this sent
actually arrived intact \(em a body mangled by the write/close-to-EOF
path would instead produce a different, distinguishable failure (a
curl-level error, or a decode failure with no real error field at
all).
.PP
.B Feedtest
calls
.BR bsky (1)'s
own
.BR decode() ,
the feed-array walk
.BR timeline() 's
curl call hands off to, directly with a hand-built JSON string in the
real
.B app.bsky.feed.getTimeline
response shape (a
.B feed
array of
.BR post / author / record
objects) \(em four posts covering a normal post, one with no
.BR author ,
one with no
.BR record ,
and one with no
.B post
at all (skipped, not a crash) \(em and checks the decoded lines
against the expected text, in the API's own order. This is a pure
function, so it needs no network.
.PP
Exits with
.B PASS
or
.B FAIL
naming what the decoded response actually held.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/cmd/bskytest.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR bsky (1)
.SH BUGS
.B Pubtest
and
.B postpubtest
need real outbound network access to
.BR public.api.bsky.app
and
.BR bsky.social ;
offline or firewalled hosts will see curl itself fail there, not a bug
in the code under test.
.B Feedtest
needs no network but covers only the fixture cases built into it, not
every shape the real API can return.
